# Automation execution source comparison

This comparison describes the existing custom workflow engine. The new native slice, resolved complete release binding and exact original module/helper observations are recorded separately in [NATIVE-SOURCE-COMPARISON.md](NATIVE-SOURCE-COMPARISON.md); the limitations below concern the earlier custom-format analysis. Reviewed 2026-10-12. The existing crosswalk nominates n8n 2.16.0, source commit `6eb2d75670b912bdc0274abd73f4f6e8ca8678c6`. Its component-version mapping is non-unique. Documentation commit `be6702d26245396df6b2fcfeb6394576a7ce3326` is a temporal snapshot before that release, not an exact availability guarantee. These limitations remain unchanged.

This implementation executes its own declarative engine. Official source was consulted as evidence; no n8n package or study reconstruction is loaded into the application's runtime. The original full n8n product has **not** been executed for these fixtures, so all original-product parity and superiority gates remain open.

| Contract area | Official pinned evidence | Implemented contract and differences |
| --- | --- | --- |
| HTTP methods, body and response | [HTTP documentation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs/be6702d26245396df6b2fcfeb6394576a7ce3326/docs/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.httprequest/index.md), sections Method, Send Body, Response and Timeout | Same documented seven methods, JSON/raw body modes, JSON/text detection and non-2xx failure unless Never Error. Our output always has an envelope under a property and retains input by default; n8n's default returns only the response body. Our timeout includes completion of body reads; the documentation describes the initial response timeout. GET/HEAD request bodies, other body formats, pagination, batching and proxy options remain unsupported. |
| HTTP defaults and credential forwarding | [HTTP V3 source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n/6eb2d75670b912bdc0274abd73f4f6e8ca8678c6/packages/nodes-base/nodes/HttpRequest/V3/HttpRequestV3.node.ts), lines 259–342 and body-processing sections | Source uses version-dependent redirect/credential-forwarding behavior and a 300,000 ms default timeout. This application uses standard Fetch redirects, strips authorization/cookies on origin changes, does not offer credential forwarding, and defaults to 10,000 ms with a 60,000 ms cap. No cookie jar, credential provider, certificate bypass or configurable redirect count. |
| Retry and error policies | [Node settings documentation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs/be6702d26245396df6b2fcfeb6394576a7ce3326/docs/workflows/components/nodes.md), Node settings; [execution source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n/6eb2d75670b912bdc0274abd73f4f6e8ca8678c6/packages/core/src/execution-engine/workflow-execute.ts), lines 1481–1583 | Stop/continue/error-output overlap the documented policies. The source retries the node and clamps enabled retries to 2–5 attempts and 0–5,000 ms. Our explicit attempts range is 1–5 with 0–10,000 ms delay; HTTP retries the individual item, other nodes the whole operation. Continue passes original node input, not a claim of matching every n8n node's last-valid-data behavior. Error output uses this application's object schema, not native item linking. |
| Wait | [Wait documentation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs/be6702d26245396df6b2fcfeb6394576a7ce3326/docs/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.wait.md), Time-based operations; [Wait source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n/6eb2d75670b912bdc0274abd73f4f6e8ca8678c6/packages/nodes-base/nodes/Wait/Wait.node.ts), lines 528–608 | n8n supports intervals, specified times, webhooks and forms; its documentation distinguishes short in-process waits from database offloading. Our integer 0–60,000 ms wait covers only a short in-process interval. There is no durable continuation, specified date, resume URL, form or webhook wait. Relative delay uses elapsed server time. Abandoned executions become interrupted rather than resumed. |
| Saved-workflow invocation | [Execute Sub-workflow documentation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n-docs/be6702d26245396df6b2fcfeb6394576a7ce3326/docs/integrations/builtin/core-nodes/n8n-nodes-base.executeworkflow.md), Source, Mode and Options; [ExecuteWorkflow source](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/n8n-io/n8n/6eb2d75670b912bdc0274abd73f4f6e8ca8678c6/packages/nodes-base/nodes/ExecuteWorkflow/ExecuteWorkflow/ExecuteWorkflow.node.ts), lines 284–469 | Saved-ID lookup, all-items and each-item modes overlap the documented synchronous modes. This application always waits and flattens selected child output arrays, with nested traces in parent history. It does not provide n8n trigger/input schemas, type conversion, detached execution, child execution IDs, paired-item metadata, local-file/URL sources or graph extraction. Recursive IDs are rejected and calls share a root deadline and budget. |

## Validation boundary

`app.test.mjs` preserves the previous transformation contracts. `execution.test.mjs` exercises synthetic loopback endpoints and the real local host API, without connecting to remote accounts or changing external data. Successful development tests establish this implementation's methods, request/response handling, error routes, retry behavior, timeout, cancellation, redaction and saved-call contracts. They do not establish original behavior equivalence, completeness, speed/reliability improvements, production security or recovery under process/storage faults.

Remaining acceptance work includes preserved original-product fixtures, native workflow exchange, credential encryption/authentication, published versions, triggers, queues, durable waits, complete integration catalog and expressions, native execution/item-linking semantics, error workflows, administration/collaboration, and comparative studies. The shared crosswalk and STATUS completion gates have not been marked complete.
